OL,24,ANext Page BNW Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,365,360,120,260,000,100
PN,36406
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F364A1786119514
OL,3,CMan admits preventing lawful burial of
OL,4,Cfatal arson attack suspect
OL,6,FA trial at Liverpool Crown Court heard
OL,7,FMr Smith had travelled with Owens to
OL,8,Fthe home in South John Street just
OL,9,Fafter 12.30am on July 15.
OL,11,FWeetman was jailed for life with a
OL,12,Fminimum of 25 years for planning the
OL,13,Fattack after Mrs Jackson's son George,
OL,14,F48, refused to sell drugs for him.
OL,16,FMaynard, said to be the "trusted
OL,17,Flieutenant" in Weetman's drugs line,
OL,18,Fwas jailed for 23 years and Owens was
OL,19,Fsentenced to 13 years and six months.
OL,26,@xD@YOUyD@KO]
